{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found it. Invoice #4471 for October pallets from Harborview Supplies (billing@harborview-supplies.example) was caught by our spam filter. I've asked for it to be delivered to your inbox. Once a technician approves that, it should show up in your inbox. Please reply to let us know when you have it. One more thing: our records show your account is locked after several failed sign-in attempts on Friday morning. If you're having trouble signing in, let us know and we can help you get back in.",
  "internal_note": "KB-007 followed. The sender is Tom Becker (user_id 4, Finance). His quarantine has Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, subject 'Invoice #4471 - October pallets', reason spam, releasable. The sender, subject and invoice number all match what the user described, and I saw no look-alike domain. I queued release_email for Q-1004 (approval id 1). It needs approval and has not run. The same quarantine also has Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, 'Scanned document 0931.zip', reason malware, not releasable. It is unrelated to this ticket and I did not touch it. Separate issue: the account status is locked with 5 failed logins. The sign-in logs show the failures on 10/09 around 09:20-09:35 ET, all from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York during his usual hours, with one Duo success in the middle. That looks like a stale saved password on a device, not an attack. The user didn't ask for an unlock, so I didn't queue one and told him to contact us if he can't sign in.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
